49
00:03:13,470 --> 00:03:15,210
And this is an important concept.

50
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:17,040
So pay close attention.

51
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:23,400
X and y coordinates are like the positions for everything that happens on the scratch stage.

52
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:27,540
This helps us know where things are and how to move them around.

53
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:34,950
Like, imagine a giant grid covering the entire scratch stage with horizontal lines and vertical lines

54
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,390
crossing each other.

55
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:39,390
The grid is made up of x and y coordinates.

56
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:45,630
The x coordinate represents the horizontal position, or the left and right position of the sprite on

57
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:51,300
the stage, and the y coordinate represents the vertical position or the up and down of the sprite on

58
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:51,990
the stage.

59
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:55,840
Now let's think of it like a like a treasure map.

60
00:03:56,110 --> 00:04:02,320
The x and y coordinates are like the instructions on how many steps to take in each direction to find

61
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,040
the treasure.

62
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:12,050
If we're told to take ten steps, right, and five steps up, we'd move ten steps along the x axis and

63
00:04:12,050 --> 00:04:15,470
five steps along the y axis and scratch.

64
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:24,080
The stage has its own coordinate system with zero x and zero y being the center point.

65
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:33,050
The x coordinates range from -240 to 240, while the y coordinates range from -180 to 180.

66
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:39,620
When you want to move a sprite to a specific spot on the stage, you simply set its x and y coordinates.

67
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:44,870
For example, let's say we want to move our cat sprite to the top right corner of the stage.

68
00:04:45,350 --> 00:04:50,570
We would then set the x coordinate to 240 and the y coordinate to 180.

69
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:59,630
You can also use the motion blocks in scratch like go to x 240 and y 180, or change y by minus five

70
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:03,530
to move your sprites around the stage using x and y coordinates.

71
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:10,310
Understanding X and Y coordinates is important for creating smooth animations and exciting games, as

72
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:16,130
it helps us position our sprites exactly where we want them on the stage, and that is why they are

73
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:17,030
so important.

